<title>GERMANY: Daimler hits all-time high after 96 figures.</title>
<headline>Daimler hits all-time high after 96 figures.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Daimler-Benz AG surged in after-bourse trade to an all-time high of 135.80 marks after the company released preliminary results for 1996.</p>
<p>The shares fell back within minutes to trade at 134.70 marks, still up 3.6 percent.</p>
<p>Daimler said in a statement it planned to pay a dividend of 1.10 marks per share on 1996 earnings, having omitted a dividend for 1995.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
